{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"halfboiled-nepotic-weaverbird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nT3 (integration feasibility) and T10 (infra/IaC) have never blocked in ~2,500 runs each — but this was a configuration artifact (blocking_enabled false, threshold 0.95), not a quality signal: 13/20 sampled T3 findings were actionable codebase-grounded criticisms (e.g. a nonexistent pydantic-ai-slim[retries] extra), and 62% of T10's strong findings cite concrete repo artifacts. The audited T10 keyword gate (infra vocabulary plus GitHub-Actions supply-chain tokens) measured 28% fire rate with 100% strong-finding recall. Operator approved enabling blocking for both.\n\n## Approach\nIn src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json: set T3 blocking_enabled true at block_threshold 0.90 (conservative pilot; the standing zero-LLM criterion-effectiveness recorder monitors outcomes for a later 0.85 revisit), and T10 blocking_enabled true at 0.90 scoped to its rubric's MAJOR classes (destructive apply, wildcard grant, plaintext secret, unauthenticated internet-reachable service). Add the audited T10 regex (including .github/workflows, pull_request_target, secrets.* tokens) to the deterministic overlay rules in registry.py so T10 runs on ~28% of reviews instead of all. Alternative rejected: enabling at 0.85 immediately — 0.90 first bounds the blast radius while the effectiveness recorder accumulates post-change data at zero LLM cost.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py, tests/llm/test_criteria_blocking.py, docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md (regenerated).\n\n## Testing\nUnit: a T3 finding at priority 0.92 produces a blocking decision and one at 0.85 stays advisory; same for T10 MAJOR-class fixtures; the T10 gate fires on a terraform-touching fixture plan and on a GHA workflow plan, and skips a pure-docs plan with a coverage record.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] T3 findings at priority >= 0.90 block; below stays advisory (checked: unit tests on Pass-3 decide).\n- [ ] T10 MAJOR-class findings at >= 0.90 block (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] The T10 DET gate fires on infra and GHA fixtures and skips non-infra plans with zero T10 LLM calls (checked: unit tests).\n- [ ] The criteria guide is regenerated reflecting both posture changes (checked: committed regen output).","id":"bfa8-51d0-3286-4779","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Enable T3 and T10 blocking and add the T10 infra DET overlay gate"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384380449166001,"uuid":"b80c68cf-9dba-439d-acbe-ac0a82c9a7de"}